-- Open question: do deck driven connection changes count towards WPWE1 and
-- WPWE2, and is WPWE1 suppressed while the well is stopped?  No CECON and no
-- WTEST, so every connection change below comes from WELOPEN alone.
--
--   B-1H  open producer, one connection shut  -> WPWE2?
--   B-2H  open producer, one connection opened-> WPWE1?
--   B-3H  stopped producer, same reopen       -> WPWE1, or gated off?
--
-- The manual qualifies WPWE1 with "if the well is not shut or stopped", so
-- B-2H against B-3H isolates that gate.  Flow reports zero for all three
-- because it absorbs deck driven changes.
--
-- Because the expected result for those three wells is silence, C-1H carries a
-- CECON CON workover as an internal control: it must report WPWE2, WPWE3 and
-- WPWE7.  Without it a run that reported nothing at all would be
-- indistinguishable from one that worked.  The control is the only economic
-- limit in the deck and touches no other well, so the three probes above stay
-- purely deck driven.

INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-model.inc' /

SUMMARY
INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-summary.inc' /

SCHEDULE
TUNING
 0.1 1.0 1.0e-4 /
 /
 /

INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-wells.inc' /

-- Part of the initial state: no timestep has elapsed, so these closures are
-- not themselves events under any reading.
WELOPEN
 'B-2H'  'SHUT'  8  7 3 2* /
 'B-3H'  'SHUT' 14 12 3 2* /
/

WCONPROD
 'B-3H' 'STOP' 'ORAT' 1500.0 4* 100.0 /
/

CECON
 'C-1H' 2* 1 5 1* 1.0 1* 'CON' /
/

TSTEP
 1 /

WELOPEN
 'B-1H'  'SHUT' 15  3 2 2* /
 'B-2H'  'OPEN'  8  7 3 2* /
 'B-3H'  'OPEN' 14 12 3 2* /
/

TSTEP
 2*1 /
END
